── FACT BEYOND A `without` LIMIT ─────── E0204_while_without_div.lt:3:3  [E0204]

This `while` loop may not end, but `count_down` says `without div`:

  1 │ fn count_down(n: i64, step: i64) -> i64 without div {
    │                                                 ─── the limit
  2 │   var i = n
  3 │   while i > 0 { i -= step }
    │   ^^^^^

A counting loop needs a statement `i -= s` of the loop's own block, with `s`
known positive.
